{
  "localOnly": true,
  "reason": "The original nonnegative-input, zero-bias Kaiming initialization leaves 36/128 first-layer units globally inactive at seed 11. Compare paired Kaiming matrices with zero, uniform and input-domain-anchored biases; uniform/domain retain identical later-layer biases. This is a controlled initialization screen, not a replacement for the original grid or 8/16-layer experiments.",
  "budget": "1000 complete epochs (10000 optimizer updates), seed 11, full mod-97 training half. AdamW and ten-update warmup; cosine decay to 0.001 of initial lr. Exact rounded accuracy and residue RMSE remain the metrics.",
  "interpretation": "Zero vs uniform changes biases in every layer. Uniform vs domain changes only the first-layer bias rule. Treat seed-11 screens as exploratory and confirm useful fixed settings on three seeds.",
